75,3469,5098,5943,6639,7303,7938],[26625,3474,5106,5952,6648,7313,7949],[26675,3480,5113,5960,6657,7323,7960],[26725,3485,5121,5968,6667,7333,7971],[26775,3490,5128,5977,6676,7344,7983],[26825,3495,5136,5985,6686,7354,7994],[26875,3500,5143,5994,6695,7364,8005],[26925,3506,5150,6002,6704,7375,8016],[26975,3511,5158,6010,6714,7385,8028],[27025,3516,5165,6019,6723,7395,8039],[27075,3521,5173,6027,6732,7406,8050],[27125,3526,5180,6036,6742,7416,8061],[27175,3532,5187,6044,6751,7426,8072],[27225,3537,5195,6052,6761,7437,8084],[27275,3542,5202,6061,6770,7447,8095],[27325,3547,5210,6069,6779,7457,8106]],"lookup":"bracket","minIncome":25,"maxIncome":27374.99,"aboveMax":{"method":"discretion","pct":null},"columnFor":null},"percent":null,"formula":null,"shared":{"method":"cross-credit","thresholdOvernights":146,"multiplier":1.5,"reductionTable":null},"addOns":{"childcare":true,"health":true},"extra":{"bracketWidth":50,"lastBracketHigh":27374.99,"minimumOrder":{"perChildMonthly":40,"maxTotalMonthly":120,"appliesAtOrBelowGrossMonthly":998,"approxNetMonthly":884,"rule":"750 ILCS 5/505(a)(3.3a); 75% of the 2026 HHS poverty guideline for one person = $998 gross a month, about $884 net (2026 Addendum p. 8)","source":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/hfs/childsupport/parents/2026addendumbosnit.pdf"},"columns":["combinedNetIncomeBracketLow (bracket = low to low+49.99)","1","2","3","4","5","6"]},"lowIncome":{"selfSupportReserve":null,"period":"monthly","minimumOrder":40,"method":"text"},"statute":{"name":"750 ILCS 5/505","url":"https://www.ilga.gov/legislation/ilcs/fulltext.asp?DocName=075000050K505"},"guidelinesUrl":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/childsupport/parents/incomeshares.html","officialCalculatorUrl":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/childsupport/parents/childsupportestimator.html","incomeDefinition":"Gross income is all income from all sources except means-tested benefits (TANF, SSI, SNAP) and benefits or income received for other children in the household; social security disability/retirement benefits paid for the subject child count in the disabled or retired parent's income (750 ILCS 5/505(a)(3)(A)). Net income is gross income minus the standardized tax amount (federal and state income tax for a single person with standard deduction, plus Social Security and Medicare; the parent with the majority of parenting time is deemed to claim the child), read from the HFS Gross to Net Income Conversion Table, or minus an individualized tax amount by stipulation or court determination (505(a)(3)(B)-(E)). Net income is then reduced by multi-family adjustments and spousal maintenance (505(a)(3)(F)).","modelText":"The HFS schedule is published as $50 income brackets (e.g. 5,975.00 - 6,024.99); 750 ILCS 5/505(a)(1.5)(C) says to select the corresponding amount for the parties' combined monthly net income, so the amount of the bracket containing the income applies.","sharedText":"750 ILCS 5/505(a)(3.8): if each parent exercises 146 or more overnights per year, the basic obligation is multiplied by 1.5; each parent's share (by percentage of combined net income) is multiplied by the percentage of time the child spends with the other parent, and the two amounts are offset, the parent owing more paying the difference. HFS publishes a Shared Physical Care Support Obligation Worksheet.","addOnsText":"court may order; prorated by share of combined net income and may be added to the basic obligation premium attributable to the child added to the basic obligation and allocated by net income 750 ILCS 5/505(a)(3.7): reasonable child care for work, education or job search is prorated by each parent's share of combined net income, minus the federal child care tax credit if allowed. (a)(4)(D)-(E): the health insurance premium attributable to the child (or premium divided by persons covered, times children covered) is added and allocated by net income; if the obligor pays it, the obligee's share is deducted from the obligor's support, if the obligee pays it, the obligor's share is added. (a)(3.6): extracurricular and school expenses may be ordered in addition.","lowIncomeText":"Low-income adjustment is built into the schedule: the 2026 Addendum says the first tier aligns with after-tax income at 75% of the 2026 FPG for one person. Below that threshold the $40-per-child minimum order applies (505(a)(3.3a)).","emancipation":{"text":"For 750 ILCS 5/505, 'child' includes any child under 18 and any child aged 19 or younger who is still attending high school.","url":"https://www.ilga.gov/legislation/ilcs/fulltext.asp?DocName=075000050K505"},"scheduleText":"The HFS schedule is published as $50 income brackets (e.g. 5,975.00 - 6,024.99); 750 ILCS 5/505(a)(1.5)(C) says to select the corresponding amount for the parties' combined monthly net income, so the amount of the bracket containing the income applies.","aboveMaxText":"750 ILCS 5/505(a)(3.5): if combined adjusted net income exceeds the highest level of the schedule, the court may use its discretion, but the basic obligation may not be less than the amount at the highest level of the schedule (bracket 27,325.00-27,374.99 in the 2026 schedule).","effective":"2026-03-20","facts":[{"text":"Illinois switched from a percentage-of-obligor-net-income guideline to income shares effective July 1, 2017 (Public Act 99-0764).","url":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/childsupport/parents/incomeshares.html"},{"text":"Since 2024 HFS updates both the Gross to Net Income Conversion Table and the Schedule of Basic Obligations every year; the current versions took effect March 20, 2026.","url":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/childsupport/parents/incomeshares.html"},{"text":"The 2026 schedule was extended to combined net income up to $27,374.99 per month (previously $26,724.99).","url":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/hfs/childsupport/parents/2026addendumbosnit.pdf"},{"text":"If a parent has insufficient work history, potential income is presumed to be 75% of the HHS poverty guideline for a family of one (505(a)(3.2a)); incarceration is not voluntary unemployment.","url":"https://www.ilga.gov/legislation/ilcs/fulltext.asp?DocName=075000050K505"},{"text":"In split physical care, two worksheets are computed as if each parent's child were the only child, and the smaller obligation is subtracted from the larger (505(a)(3.9)).","url":"https://www.ilga.gov/legislation/ilcs/fulltext.asp?DocName=075000050K505"}],"sources":[{"name":"Illinois: 750 ILCS 5/505","url":"https://www.ilga.gov/legislation/ilcs/fulltext.asp?DocName=075000050K505"},{"name":"Illinois: child support guidelines","url":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/childsupport/parents/incomeshares.html"},{"name":"Illinois: official schedule of basic support obligations","url":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/hfs/childsupport/parents/2026ilschedofbobligations.pdf"},{"name":"Illinois: shared parenting rule","url":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/hfs/sitecollectiondocuments/standalonesharedphysicalcaresupportobligationworksheet.pdf"},{"name":"Illinois: low-income rule","url":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/content/dam/soi/en/web/hfs/childsupport/parents/2026addendumbosnit.pdf"},{"name":"Illinois: official child support calculator","url":"https://hfs.illinois.gov/childsupport/parents/childsupportestimator.html"}],"testCases":[{"inputs":{"incomeA":4000,"incomeB":2000,"children":2,"overnightsA":0},"expected":1205.33,"what":"parent A's monthly share of the basic child support obligation (net incomes)","source":"Computed by hand from the 2026 HFS schedule: combined net $6,000 falls in bracket 5,975.00-6,024.99, two children = $1,808; A's share 4000/6000; 1808 x 2/3 = 1205.33. No official worked example on the HFS schedule."},{"inputs":{"incomeA":4000,"incomeB":2000,"children":2,"overnightsA":146,"overnightsB":219},"expected":723.2,"what":"monthly transfer from parent A under shared physical care (505(a)(3.8)), no add-ons","source":"Computed by hand following the HFS Shared Physical Care worksheet: 1808 x 1.5 = 2712; A 2712 x 2/3 x 219/365 = 1084.80; B 2712 x 1/3 x 146/365 = 361.60; difference 723.20."},{"inputs":{"incomeA":800,"incomeB":3000,"children":2,"overnightsA":0},"expected":80,"what":"payer's monthly minimum order ($40 per child) when the payer's income is at or below 75% of the poverty guideline","source":"Computed by hand from 750 ILCS 5/505(a)(3.3a): 2 x $40 = $80. The calculator treats a payer net income at or below about $884 a month (2026 Addendum: 75% of the 2026 FPG = $998 gross, about $884 net) as within the rule."}]}